## 10. Model Selection Rule

### 10.1 One-Standard-Error (1-SE) Rule

The 1-SE threshold was computed as:
Threshold = CV R²_best − SD_best / √k

Where:
- `CV R²_best` = 0.8241 (highest cross-validated R², achieved by SVR)
- `SD_best` = 0.0136 (standard deviation of SVR's CV R²)
- `k` = 5 (number of folds)
**Calculation:**
Threshold = 0.8241 − 0.0136 / √5 = 0.8241 − 0.0061 = 0.8180

### 10.2 Models Within 1-SE

| Model | CV R² Mean | CV R² SD | Within 1-SE? |
|-------|-----------|----------|--------------|
| SVR | 0.8241 | 0.0136 | Yes |
| Ridge | 0.8203 | 0.0088 | Yes |
| ElasticNet | 0.8200 | 0.0097 | Yes |
| XGBoost | 0.8132 | 0.0192 | No |
| Linear Regression | 0.8084 | 0.0173 | No |
| Gradient Boosting | 0.7954 | 0.0328 | No |
| Random Forest | 0.7932 | 0.0151 | No |
| Baseline Mean | −0.0574 | 0.1065 | No |

### 10.3 Parsimony Rule

Among models within the 1-SE threshold, the model with the **fewest tuned hyperparameters** was selected.

| Model | Hyperparameters Tuned | Parsimony Rank | Selected? |
|-------|----------------------|----------------|-----------|
| Ridge | 1 (`alpha`) | 1 | **Yes** |
| ElasticNet | 2 (`alpha`, `l1_ratio`) | 2 | No |
| SVR | 3 (`C`, `epsilon`, `kernel`) | 3 | No |

**Final model: Ridge Regression** (selected by the pre-specified 1-SE plus parsimony rule, not by test-set superiority)

