## 13. Feature Importance

### 13.1 Method

**Held-out permutation importance** was computed on the final Ridge Regression model, evaluated on the chronological test set.

**Rationale:** This model-agnostic approach avoids the incomparability of coefficient magnitudes, impurity-based importances, and model-specific scores across the six algorithms.

### 13.2 Results

| Feature | Importance Mean | Importance SD |
|---------|-----------------|---------------|
| Cultivated_Area_ha | 1.180515 | 0.112767 |
| Soil_Type | 0.072618 | 0.018213 |
| Fertilizer_Used | 0.007901 | 0.004950 |
| pH | 0.006587 | 0.006184 |
| Exchangeable_K_ppm | 0.002232 | 0.006203 |
| Available_P_ppm | 0.000743 | 0.000910 |
| Relative_Humidity_percent | 0.000474 | 0.000339 |
| Precipitation_mm_day | 0.000243 | 0.000612 |
| Annual_Temperature_C | 0.000160 | 0.001730 |
| Organic_C_percent | −0.000064 | 0.005863 |
| Total_N_percent | −0.000902 | 0.002331 |
| Solar_Radiation_MJ_m2_day | −0.001148 | 0.000600 |
| Soil_Wetness | −0.002113 | 0.001587 |
| Wind_Speed_m_s | −0.004955 | 0.002646 |

### 13.3 Cultivated Area Contribution

To quantify the contribution of cultivated area, Ridge was re-fitted without `Cultivated_Area_ha`:

| Model | Test R² |
|-------|---------|
| Full model (with cultivated area) | 0.8409 |
| Reduced model (without cultivated area) | 0.6192 |
| **Drop in R²** | **0.2217** |

**Interpretation:** Cultivated area dominates prediction. However, this dominance partly reflects the mechanical relationship between cultivated area and total production (production ≈ area × yield). These are predictive associations, not causal determinants.

### 13.4 Interpretation of Negative Importance

Small negative values indicate that shuffling a feature marginally improved test performance. This is interpreted as the **absence of a detectable predictive signal** rather than as active harm.

