## 15. Limitations

The findings should be interpreted within the following constraints:

| Limitation | Description | Implication |
|------------|-------------|-------------|
| **Limited geographic scope** | Five districts over a single 16-year period (N = 500) | Generalizability to other districts/regions is limited |
| **No external validation** | External temporal and spatial validation not performed | Results do not constitute operational forecast validation |
| **Secondary data quality** | Data from district offices may contain measurement inconsistencies | Some uncertainty in predictor values |
| **Omitted variables** | Socio-economic and farm-management variables not included | Model may not capture all production drivers |
| **Retrospective design** | Same-year cultivated area and full-year weather summaries not available at forecast time | Framework is retrospective estimation, not operational forecasting |
| **No spatial transfer test** | Leave-one-district-out validation not performed (no observation-level district identifier) | Spatial transfer to unseen districts untested |
| **Overlapping CIs** | Bootstrap CIs overlap substantially among top models | Small performance differences should not be over-interpreted |
| **Dominant predictor** | Cultivated area dominates prediction | Partly reflects mechanical relationship with total production |

### 15.1 Future Work

Future research should:

1. Integrate larger datasets covering additional districts and years
2. Incorporate remote-sensing variables
3. Include socio-economic and farm-management information
4. Perform external temporal and spatial validation
5. Develop operational forecasting models using lagged and seasonal predictors
6. Test spatial transfer using leave-one-district-out validation

